import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Doon Challengers Club" description="Doon Challengers Club — a football and volleyball club for underprivileged youth, organized by Sarvagun Society in Dehradun.">
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[var(--spacing-page)] px-4 lg:px-6">
      <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-heading font-bold mb-6">Doon Challengers Club</h1>
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-text-muted space-y-4">
        <p>In today's fast-growing technology, the youth are losing sportsmanship. With cricket considered as a "second God" in India, other sports like Hockey, Football, and Volleyball are getting neglected.</p>

        <p>Keeping this in mind, Sarvagun Society formed a football and volleyball club named <strong>Doon Challengers</strong>. The club participates in various tournaments in the state and districts.</p>

        <p>The society selects boys who are good at sports but, due to weak financial conditions, could not afford to play. The society provides dress kits to every member and motivates them to improve their skills.</p>

        <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-xl text-primary mt-8">Swami Vivekananda Football Tournament</h3>
        <p>Following the footsteps of Swami Vivekananda, whose birthday is celebrated as <strong>National Youth Day</strong>, the society started a knock-out football tournament from 1 January 2011. It is a running trophy held every year.</p>

        <p>In the first edition, 14 registered football clubs and 2 Gorkha Regiments participated. Altogether 15 matches were played. The final match was played on Swami Vivekananda's Birthday (12 January).</p>

        <p>The final event was headed by Dr. Dhirendra Sharma (scientist), with Chief Guest Sri Tarun Vijay (MP, Rajya Sabha). <strong>Doon Star</strong> won the trophy by 3-0.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
